## `emit(v)`: a string is written, anything else is one byte, the low 8 bits of the INTEGER v. The byte path reads v
## through __rt_uint (it changes %rax only, so the length in %rcx survives): it used to shift the word right by one
## without looking at it, so an integer that lives in a cell (beyond 63 bits) emitted a byte of its ADDRESS and a
## list or a record was emitted as a byte instead of being the type error it is.
fn rt_output() = ""

